===== root =====
Browse and search AI agent conversation history

Usage: aghist [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  export     Export a session to Markdown, JSON, or HTML
  index      Build or refresh the search index. Idempotent and delta-aware
  search     Search indexed sessions for a query
  health     Machine-readable doctor: validates index, manifest, and provider state
  sources    Inspect detected provider sources, or manage the remote-source registry
  show       Resolve a citation ref `<provider>/<session-id>#<turn>` to one message
  diff       Compare two sessions turn-by-turn in diff-hunk style
  track      Track how a topic evolved across sessions (LLM-required)
  decisions  Heuristic-extract candidate architectural decisions from sessions
  mcp        Run a stdio MCP server exposing aghist's read paths to agents
  schema     Emit JSON-Schema (draft-2020-12) for an aghist subcommand
  todos      Surface unresolved TODOs / follow-ups / open bd refs across sessions
  threads    Cluster sessions into "threads" of related work
  note       Manage per-user notes attached to sessions or turns
  tag        Manage per-user tags attached to sessions or turns
  star       Mark a session or turn as starred
  unstar     Remove a star from a session or turn. Errors with `star-not-found` if the ref is not currently starred
  stars      List starred sessions and turns
  usage      Aggregate token usage and (when pricing is known) USD cost across sessions
  project    Per-project productivity dashboard
  report     Cross-project weekly summary suitable for journals or reviews
  update     Update a self-managed release binary to the latest GitHub release
  uninstall  Remove a self-managed release binary and data
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --list             List sessions without opening the TUI
      --limit <LIMIT>    Maximum number of sessions to return when paired with `--list`. JSON output includes `meta.next_cursor` if more results remain [default: 20]
      --cursor <CURSOR>  Opaque pagination cursor (from a prior `meta.next_cursor`) for `--list`
      --reindex          Force rebuild the search index
      --json             Force JSON output (for one-shot commands like --list, export). Mutually exclusive with --ndjson
      --ndjson           Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json
      --provider <SLUG>  Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`
      --since <RFC3339>  RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`
      --until <RFC3339>  RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)
      --project <NAME>   Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)
      --role <ROLE>      Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`
      --has-tool-call    Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content
      --note <SUBSTR>    Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)
      --tag <NAME>       Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar
      --starred          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

===== export =====
Export a session to Markdown, JSON, or HTML

Usage: aghist export [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>          Output format: md, json, html
  -s, --session <SESSION>        Session ID/prefix, `<provider>/<id>`, or `<source>:<provider>/<id>` to export
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>          Output file path (defaults to stdout)
      --turn-range <TURN_RANGE>  Slice the session by 1-based turn range (e.g. `12:25`, `:10`, `5:`, or `7`). Bounds are inclusive. Out-of-range bounds clamp to the available messages
      --include-notes            Inline private annotations (notes from the metadata sidecar) at their citation refs. Session-level notes render once near the top; turn-level notes render after the message they're attached to. Notes stay marked "private annotation" so consumers don't conflate them with session content. No-op when the metadata sidecar is absent or has no matching notes
      --json                     Force JSON output (for one-shot commands like --list, export). Mutually exclusive with --ndjson
      --ndjson                   Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json
      --params <JSON>            JSON request body containing all params at once. Mutually exclusive with other flags. Schema: `{format, session, output?, turn_range?, include_notes?}`. Lets agents skip per-flag discovery and submit a single JSON request
      --provider <SLUG>          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`
      --since <RFC3339>          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`
      --until <RFC3339>          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)
      --project <NAME>           Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)
      --role <ROLE>              Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`
      --has-tool-call            Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content
      --note <SUBSTR>            Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)
      --tag <NAME>               Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar
      --starred                  Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar
  -h, --help                     Print help

===== index =====
Build or refresh the search index. Idempotent and delta-aware.

Skips sessions whose source files are unchanged since the last run, re-indexes those that have changed, and indexes any new sessions. Always exits with status 0 on success and prints a JSON summary of `added` / `updated` / `unchanged` counts to stdout.

Usage: aghist index [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --provider <PROVIDER>
          Reindex only sessions from this provider (`claude-code`, `copilot-cli`, `gemini-cli`, `codex-cli`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `aider`, `zed-ai`, `cline`, `continue-dev`)

      --force
          Force a full rebuild by clearing the index first

      --accept-download
          Authorise the one-off download of the embedding model (~90 MB `AllMiniLML6V2`). Required the first time semantic indexing runs; consent is persisted next to the index, so subsequent runs don't need this flag. Without consent (and without this flag), indexing stays purely lexical

      --params <JSON>
          JSON request body containing all params at once. Mutually exclusive with other flags. Schema: `{provider?, force?, accept_download?}`

      --json
          Force JSON output (for one-shot commands like --list, export). Mutually exclusive with --ndjson

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

      --note <SUBSTR>
          Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)

      --tag <NAME>
          Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar

      --starred
          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== search =====
Search indexed sessions for a query

Usage: aghist search [OPTIONS] [QUERY]

Arguments:
  [QUERY]
          Tantivy query string (matches content + project fields).
          
          Omit when reading the query from `--query-file`, `--stdin`, or `--params`.

Options:
      --query-file <PATH>
          Read the query from a file (use `-` for stdin).
          
          Useful for queries containing shell metacharacters (quotes, braces, etc.) without escaping. Trailing whitespace is stripped.

      --stdin
          Read the query from standard input (read until EOF).
          
          Useful for queries containing shell metacharacters (quotes, braces, etc.) without escaping. Trailing whitespace is stripped.

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of hits to return
          
          [default: 20]

      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Opaque pagination cursor from a prior `meta.next_cursor`

      --json
          Force JSON output (default: JSON on pipe, table on TTY)

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --watch
          Long-running stream: emit one NDJSON line per new hit as sessions land.
          
          First poll backfills all existing matches up to `--limit`, then each subsequent poll emits only previously-unseen `(session_id, message_id)` hits. Useful for an "agent of agents" watching another agent's progress. Output is NDJSON regardless of TTY; `--json` is implied.

      --provider <SLUG>
          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`

      --watch-interval-ms <MS>
          Poll interval in milliseconds when `--watch` is set (default 2000)
          
          [default: 2000]

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --watch-iterations <N>
          Stop watch mode after N polls (0 = run until interrupted; default 0).
          
          Mostly useful for tests and one-shot snapshots.
          
          [default: 0]

      --debug-search
          Show BM25 score breakdown per result (Tantivy explanation tree). Useful for tuning relevance and surfacing ranking surprises

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --hybrid-weight <FLOAT>
          Reciprocal Rank Fusion weight on the semantic side, in `[0.0, 1.0]`.
          
          `0.0` (default) -> lexical-only BM25, identical to omitting the flag. `0.5` -> equal RRF blend of BM25 and `FastEmbed` cosine ranks. `1.0` -> semantic-only.
          
          Fails open: if the binary lacks the `embeddings` feature, or no consent / embedding store exists yet, the search degrades to lexical-only regardless of this value (see `meta.engine` in JSON output). When hybrid is active, `score` becomes the RRF fused score (small, ~0-0.03) - not a BM25 score.
          
          [default: 0]

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --params <JSON>
          JSON request body containing all params at once. Mutually exclusive with other flags. Schema: `{query, limit?, json?, hybrid_weight?}`. The `query` field carries the literal query string; use `--query-file` / `--stdin` for file/stdin input

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

      --note <SUBSTR>
          Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)

      --tag <NAME>
          Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar

      --starred
          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== health =====
Machine-readable doctor: validates index, manifest, and provider state.

Exits 0 if all checks pass (or only warn), 1 if any check fails. The JSON envelope is `{ok, checks:[{name, status, hint?}], summary}` so agents can branch on individual check kinds.

Usage: aghist health [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Force JSON output (for one-shot commands like --list, export). Mutually exclusive with --ndjson

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

