===== diff =====
Compare two sessions turn-by-turn in diff-hunk style.

Computes the longest-common-subsequence of the two sessions' messages (keyed by role + first-64-chars of content) and emits hunks of diverging turns, with 2 lines of shared context around each hunk. Useful for "compare yesterday's debug session with today's working one".

Session refs: `<provider>/<session-id>` (no turn suffix).

Usage: aghist diff [OPTIONS] <SESSION1> <SESSION2>

Arguments:
  <SESSION1>
          First session ref (e.g. `claude-code/abc-123` or `laptop:claude-code/abc-123`)

  <SESSION2>
          Second session ref (e.g. `claude-code/def-456` or `laptop:claude-code/def-456`)

Options:
  -c, --context <N>
          Context lines around each changed hunk (default 2)
          
          [default: 2]

      --json
          Force JSON output (default: unified diff text on TTY, JSON on pipe)

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --provider <SLUG>
          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

