===== todos =====
Surface unresolved TODOs / follow-ups / open bd refs across sessions.

Heuristic-first scan: looks for `TODO`, `follow-up`, `come back to`, `we should`, and beads-style refs (e.g. `ahist-y3o.7.2`). Each match becomes one candidate keyed by a citation ref so the caller can `aghist show` or quote the originating turn. No LLM, no `bd` lookups — agents can post-process (e.g. drop refs whose `bd show` reports closed).

Pass `--llm` to route the heuristic candidates through a Claude Messages API call that returns structured records of the form `{description, raised_at: ref, target_session?, status_inferred}`. Configured via env (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` / `AGHIST_LLM_API_KEY`, `AGHIST_LLM_ENDPOINT`, `AGHIST_LLM_MODEL`); the system prompt is sent with `cache_control: ephemeral` to cap re-invocation cost.

Usage: aghist todos [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --kind <KIND>
          Restrict to one or more kinds. Repeat the flag, or comma-separate. Valid: `todo`, `follow-up`, `come-back-to`, `we-should`, `bd-ref`

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of candidates to emit (0 = no limit)
          
          [default: 200]

      --json
          Force JSON output (default: JSON on pipe, table on TTY)

      --llm
          Route heuristic candidates through an LLM for structured extraction (`description` / `target_session` / `status_inferred`). Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (or `AGHIST_LLM_API_KEY`)

      --llm-model <MODEL>
          Override the LLM model id (default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 or `AGHIST_LLM_MODEL`). Only meaningful with `--llm`

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --provider <SLUG>
          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

      --note <SUBSTR>
          Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)

      --tag <NAME>
          Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar

      --starred
          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== threads =====
Cluster sessions into "threads" of related work.

Default heuristic: bucket sessions by `project_name`, then walk each bucket chronologically — sessions cluster when their gap is within `--gap-hours` (default 4h). Useful for "what's the history on feature X across multiple sessions?".

Pass `--llm` to route session digests through a Claude Messages API call that groups by semantic topic *across project boundaries*. The heuristic can't cross projects; the LLM can. Configured via env (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` / `AGHIST_LLM_API_KEY`, `AGHIST_LLM_ENDPOINT`, `AGHIST_LLM_MODEL`); the system prompt is sent with `cache_control: ephemeral` to cap re-invocation cost.

Usage: aghist threads [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --gap-hours <HOURS>
          Cluster gap in hours. Sessions in the same project within this gap merge into one thread; longer gaps split. Ignored with `--llm`
          
          [default: 4]

      --min-sessions <N>
          Drop threads with fewer than this many sessions. Ignored with `--llm`
          
          [default: 1]

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of threads to emit (0 = no limit)
          
          [default: 50]

      --json
          Force JSON output (default: JSON on pipe, table on TTY)

      --llm
          Route session digests through an LLM for semantic topic clustering across project boundaries. Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (or `AGHIST_LLM_API_KEY`)

      --llm-model <MODEL>
          Override the LLM model id (default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 or `AGHIST_LLM_MODEL`). Only meaningful with `--llm`

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --llm-max-sessions <N>
          Cap on session digests sent to the LLM (most recent kept). One digest is ~150 bytes, so 200 input is roughly 7.5K tokens per call. Only meaningful with `--llm`
          
          [default: 200]

      --provider <SLUG>
          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

      --note <SUBSTR>
          Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)

      --tag <NAME>
          Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar

      --starred
          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

