===== note =====
Manage per-user notes attached to sessions or turns.

Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db` by default; override with `AGHIST_METADATA_DB`). Each note is keyed by a session ref of the form `<provider>/<session-id>` (session-level), `<provider>/<session-id>#<turn>` (turn-level), or the same shapes prefixed with `<source>:` for remote-source sessions. aghist never mutates the underlying provider history files.

Usage: aghist note [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Attach a new note to a session ref. The body is read from `--body`, `--body-file`, or stdin (`--stdin`). Outputs the created note as JSON (single object) on stdout
  list    List notes, optionally filtered by session ref
  edit    Replace the body of an existing note
  remove  Remove a note by id. Outputs the deleted row as JSON on stdout
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Force JSON output (for one-shot commands like --list, export). Mutually exclusive with --ndjson

      --ndjson
          Force newline-delimited JSON output (for streaming commands). Mutually exclusive with --json

      --provider <SLUG>
          Restrict to a single provider slug, e.g. `claude-code` or `codex-cli`

      --since <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 lower bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive). Example: `--since 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z`

      --until <RFC3339>
          RFC 3339 upper bound on message/session timestamp (inclusive)

      --project <NAME>
          Substring match against the session's project name (case-insensitive)

      --role <ROLE>
          Restrict to messages with this role: `user`, `assistant`, or `tool`

      --has-tool-call
          Keep only messages (or sessions containing messages) that include a tool invocation. Has no effect on session-level lookups that do not load message content

      --note <SUBSTR>
          Keep only sessions that have a user note whose body contains this substring (case-insensitive). Matches notes attached to the session itself or to any of its turns. Notes live in the metadata sidecar (`~/.local/share/aghist/metadata.db`; `AGHIST_METADATA_DB` overrides)

      --tag <NAME>
          Keep only sessions that have this exact tag attached (session-level OR on any of its turns). Tags live in the same metadata sidecar

      --starred
          Keep only sessions that have at least one star (session-level OR on any of its turns). Stars live in the same metadata sidecar

