===== tag =====
Manage per-user tags attached to sessions or turns.

Tags live in the metadata sidecar (same database as `aghist note`). Each tag is a short label (e.g. `review`, `todo`) attached to a session ref of the form `<provider>/<session-id>`, `<provider>/<session-id>#<turn>`, or the same shapes prefixed with `<source>:` for remote-source sessions. The (`session_ref`, `tag`) pair is unique: adding the same tag twice is a no-op error. aghist never mutates the underlying provider history files.

Usage: aghist tag [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Attach a tag to a session ref. Outputs the created row as JSON on stdout. Adding the same (ref, tag) pair twice raises a `tag-conflict` error
  list    List tags, optionally filtered by session ref and/or tag value
  remove  Detach a tag from a session ref. Outputs the deleted row as JSON
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
